n is $f(t-3)=sin\\,(5(t-3)).$\n\nFrom the shifted function, we can deduce the original unshifted function $f(t)$ by simply replacing $(t-3)$ with $t:$\n\n$$\nf(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t).\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the Laplace transform $F(s)$ of the unshifted function:\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)}=\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+25}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the shifting theorem formula $L{u(t-a)\\,f(t-a)}={e}^{-as}F(s)$ by multiplying $F(s)$ by the exponential delay factor ${e}^{-3s}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{u(t-3)sin\\,(5(t-3))} & ={e}^{-3s}\\cdot F(s) \\\\  & ={e}^{-3s}\\cdot \\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d22ba3ca-cf7a-5a77-abf6-8620076552bb" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Alternative Form of the Second Shifting Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95b42ef6-d597-5334-b33c-957c6261cde2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2s}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377119} {:answer/id #uuid "5e67f589-75f0-57c5-85af-22340fd6610b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4s}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377120} {:answer/id #uuid "c87683ee-ccf3-5912-a4df-ca5b010935d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4s}\\cdot \\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377121} {:answer/id #uuid "4c47a1e3-71ba-50fe-ad63-98d6c6590ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4s}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377122} {:answer/id #uuid "bbdf9786-1b6f-52d0-9c87-1c3595975f4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4s}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbdf9786-1b6f-52d0-9c87-1c3595975f4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4s}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{2}+4}" :db/id #